INV-komoj seeds a lifted caller only on the variables its call binds at the
result positions the value occupies. Go's def/use extractor drops the
blank, so `_, err := get()` bound ("err",) against an arity of two, the
position rule could not read it, and the fallback seeded err -- which the
caller returns, so the lift climbed the error chain.

The first cut (#1797, reverted by #1799) put `_` into stmt_defuse's
defines as a placeholder; the 2026-10-21 concept audit found two consumers
reading it as a variable (false violated on `_, err := get();
fmt.Println(err)` and `s, _ := tok.(string)`). This one keeps them apart:

- DefUseResult/CfgStatement.targets: the left-hand side by position, None
  for a slot that binds nothing; Go's short-var and assignment handlers
  report it when a blank is present and every other target names exactly
  one variable.
- RepoDdg.stmt_targets carries those positions to propagate_taint_ddg;
  stmt_defuse's defines stay the variables bound.
- _received_seeds reads positions where present and returns an EMPTY set
  only when every call line was read and every received slot is a blank;
  the walk reads that as "carries nothing", never as source_undefined.

CLI (host_secret -> subprocess): the two audit shapes stay exit 3; the
WI-sitaf repro (wrap: `_, err := get(); return "ls", err`) goes from a
false violated to exit 3. Corpus A/B (dev f02ac77359; runc, gin, coredns,
buildah): 0 verdicts moved; buildah walks None 1238 -> 1204, True 1635 ->
1524, False 1 -> 21 (each new False a value received into a blank);
host-secret-no-network evidence 91 -> 79; the other three repos' walks
identical.

